       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 30 mg is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and shock. Overdose can cause prolonged vasodilation that is hard to reverse. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n- **A typo or a unit slip:** I can enter 10 mg PO once daily. I can also enter 5 mg PO once daily, which is the usual starting dose, or 2.5 mg for a frail patient.\n- **A deliberate supratherapeutic dose:** Tell me the clinical rationale and confirm that you want it. I'll enter it with a note flagging it as above the maximum dose, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n- **A different drug or regimen:** Tell me which one, and I'll enter that instead."
      }
     ],
